  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      185.85,
      226.97,
      377.85,
      250.31
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE CODE OF CRIMINAL PROCEDUREACT, NO. 15 OF 1979",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      262.97,
      401.91,
      286.31
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      298.97,
      401.88,
      322.31
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Code of CriminalProcedure (Amendment) Act, No. of 2021.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      334.97,
      401.89,
      382.31
    ],
    "text": "2.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after section 43A of the Code of CriminalProcedure Act, No. 15 of 1979 and shall have effect assection 43B of that Act:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      394.97,
      401.89,
      502.31
    ],
    "text": "43B. (1) It shall be the duty of everyMagistrate to visit every police station situatedwithin the judicial division in respect of whichhe is appointed, at least once in every month toensure that the suspects under the police custodyat such police stations are protected to the extentprovided for in the Convention Against Tortureand other Cruel, Inhuman or DegradingTreatment or Punishment Act, No. 22 of 1994.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      514.97,
      401.88,
      538.31
    ],
    "text": "(2) For the purpose of subsection (1), theMagistrate who visits the police station, shall-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      222.57,
      550.97,
      401.88,
      598.31
    ],
    "text": "(a) personally see the suspect, and look intohis well-being, welfare and conditionsunder which he is kept at such policestation; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      222.57,
      610.97,
      401.85,
      634.31
    ],
    "text": "(b) record his observations and anycomplaint the suspect may make.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      215.85,
      646.97,
      401.89,
      670.31
    ],
    "text": "(3) Where the Magistrate is of the opinion,that the suspect may have been subjected to",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      301.03,
      441.58,
      310.1
    ],
    "text": "Short title",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      336.67,
      448.29,
      384.14
    ],
    "text": "Insertion ofnew section43B in Act,No. 15 of1979",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      143.85,
      395.11,
      209.86,
      432.98
    ],
    "text": "\u201cDuty ofMagistrates tovisit policestations10",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
